      "genus": "Haworthiopsis",
      "common_name": "Haworthiopsis",
      "description": "<em>Haworthiopsis</em> was segregated from <em>Haworthia</em> in 2013 and contains about 30 species of the harder-leaved, more xeric-adapted forms — what were formerly called section Hexangulares within the old genus. Species typically have firm, upright, often white-striped or windowed leaves. Popular windowsill succulents requiring slightly more light than <em>Haworthia</em> in the strict sense.",
      "meta_title": "Haworthiopsis — South African Rosette Succulents",
